    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d671">

                <pb facs="0862" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg750"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/2064</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tampico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-07T18:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to petroleum tax law just republished, oil companies have been
                    warned that persons highly connected with the Mexican Government are prepared to
                    profit from any refusal or failure to comply with its provisions on the ground
                    of their unconstitutionality, by promptly denouncing through third parties
                    valuable oil properties not manifested by present holders within time
                    allowed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
